# Test seams in production C# (Grid Dungeon)

`GridDungeon.Runtime` / `GridDungeon.UI` ship **internal** test helpers today (`*ForTests`, `InternalsVisibleTo("GridDungeon.Tests")`). That is allowed — not a license to grow prod types for every fixture.

Authority: [Assets/Tests/README.md](../../Assets/Tests/README.md) (Edit Mode domains and conventions; Test Runner is the fixture list), [ADR 039](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/decisions/039-uitk-dotween-show-hide.md) §5 (UITK tween simulators).

## Decision order (before adding prod code for a test)

1. **Core + Edit Mode** — generic simulators belong in `GridDungeon.Core` and `Assets/Tests/<Domain>/`. Campaign/story **behavior** belongs in `GridDungeon.Campaign` — see `unity-core-campaign-assembly.mdc`. Do not add presenter/runtime seams to test math or phase maps.
2. **Public behavior** — assert through existing commands, events, steady BEM classes, `IsSettling`, `ICentralizedUiSurface` lifecycle. Prefer panel-attached presenter setup over detached shortcuts when testing exit races ([centralized-ui-gotchas § Edit Mode without panel](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-design-docs/blob/main/docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-gotchas.md#edit-mode-tests-without-a-panel)).
3. **Shared UITK simulators** — reuse `UiTransitionSession.CompleteImmediatelyForTests`, `*Transition.SimulateDue*ForTests` ([`uitk-bem-transition.mdc`](uitk-bem-transition.mdc)). Do not fork schedule/tween completion per presenter.
4. **`internal *ForTests` on prod type** — last resort for UITK build wiring, deferred `schedule.Execute`, or state tests cannot reach without `InternalsVisibleTo`. One narrow method; name ends in `ForTests`.
5. **Manual / Play Mode** — visual feel, scene wiring, or one-off layout when Edit Mode cannot own it ([`ticket-test-documentation.mdc`](ticket-test-documentation.mdc)).

## `#if UNITY_EDITOR` in production Runtime — stop and ask first

**Before** adding `#if UNITY_EDITOR`, `using UnityEditor`, or `EditorApplication.*` under `Assets/Scripts/` **outside** `Assets/Scripts/Editor/`:

1. **Stop and ask the user** — propose an alternative and wait for confirmation.
2. **Default:** do not add editor-only branches to fix Edit Mode tests.

| OK without asking | Ask first (usually reject) |
|-------------------|----------------------------|
| `Assets/Scripts/Editor/**` | `#if UNITY_EDITOR` in Runtime / UI / Core / Campaign |
| `Application.isPlaying` for real play vs edit (destroy, material assign, tweens) | `EditorApplication.isPlaying` in Runtime to branch test vs play |
| `#if UNITY_EDITOR \|\| DEVELOPMENT_BUILD` **logging only** | Editor-only code path that changes gameplay, UI, or assets “for tests” |

**Prefer instead of editor `if` in Runtime:**

- **Core** simulators + `Assets/Tests/<Domain>/` for logic under test
- **Explicit clone from `sharedMaterials`** + assign (`sharedMaterials` edit, `materials` setter play) — never `.materials` **getter** in edit mode
- **`internal *ForTests`** on the prod type (narrow, documented) — not `#if UNITY_EDITOR` wrappers
- **Test doubles** in test asm / `GridDungeon.Tests` helpers — not Runtime public types

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — editor branch in Runtime for Edit Mode tests
#if UNITY_EDITOR
if (!EditorApplication.isPlaying) { … }
#endif

// ✅ GOOD — play vs edit runtime rule (legitimate prod)
if (Application.isPlaying)
    renderer.materials = instances;
else
    renderer.sharedMaterials = instances;
```

## Do not

| Avoid | Use instead |
|-------|-------------|
| `public` methods/properties **only** for tests | `internal` + existing `InternalsVisibleTo`; or test via public API |
| Business logic in `*ForTests` helpers | Core simulator or presenter path under test |
| Duplicate seam per presenter (`FlushScheduledFooForTests` × N) | Shared transition helper or test fixture base in `Assets/Tests/` |
| `#if UNITY_INCLUDE_TESTS` / test-only branches in prod | `internal` helpers (ship in player builds but not callable outside test asmdefs) |
| `#if UNITY_EDITOR` in Runtime/UI to satisfy tests | Ask user; Core, `Application.isPlaying`, or test asm (see above) |
| Prod hot path reads `*ForTests` properties | Neutral prod API (`CurrentAlpha`) or injection at fixture setup |
| `EnsureBuiltForTests` when normal `Show`/`OnEnable` builds tree | Call production entry point in test setup |
| New seam to skip animation when ADR 039 helper exists | `SimulateDue*ForTests` on the transition target |

## Allowed patterns (existing)

```csharp
// ✅ UITK — shared Runtime helper (ADR 039)
PopInTransition.SimulateDueExitCompletionForTests(host);

// ✅ Presenter — internal, test-only name, minimal surface
internal void EnsureBuiltForTests() { … }
internal VisualElement? HostRootForTests => m_hostRoot;
```

```csharp
// ❌ Public test hook
public void SetContextForTests(InventoryContext ctx) => …;

// ❌ Prod method encodes test scenario
internal void OpenCombatItemForTests(PartyBag bag) { … } // prefer public OpenCombatItem if real API
```

## PR / agent checklist

- [ ] Rule under test could move to **Core** — move it before adding `*ForTests`
- [ ] New `*ForTests` is **`internal`**, suffixed `ForTests`, smallest API
- [ ] No new `#if UNITY_EDITOR` / `UnityEditor` in Runtime without **user approval**
- [ ] Prod path does not read `*ForTests` properties — neutral API or injection
- [ ] UITK motion uses **ADR 039** helpers before new presenter flush/advance methods
- [ ] Test plan names **Edit Mode** path (`Tests → <Domain> → <Fixture>`)
